{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "decision": "docs/adr/0559-duckdb-in-the-publisher-runs-every-transform-and-query-spark-keeps-only-table-maintenance-and-a-transform-moves-only-on-an-engine-equality-verdict.md",
  "purpose": "Single source of truth for the DuckDB extension files a release carries beside the publisher (root ADR-0559 §6). The publisher's bundled DuckDB reads Bronze objects and Iceberg tables on R2 through them, loaded by path from the release and never downloaded at run time: automatic install and load stay off (root ADR-0127). The release build fetches each pinned download through scripts/ci/fetch_pinned.py, unpacks it, holds the file to the digest and size below, puts it under `directory` in the release's files, and then runs that release's own publisher with no network (`verify-lakehouse-engine-extensions`) before anything is signed; release admission holds the installed files to this contract again. A build of an extension only loads into the DuckDB it was built for, so `duckdb_version` and the platform key are what the bundled DuckDB must report, and raising the `duckdb` crate means raising every pin here in the same pull request.",
  "duckdb_version": "v2.0.0",
  "platforms_reason": "Each distribution pins a file per platform, named as the publisher names its own (`<os>-<arch>` of the Rust target): linux-x86_64 for the data host's release, linux-aarch64 for the AWS images (Graviton, root ADR-0619 §7). The four arm64 files carry the same extension builds as the x86 ones (each file's metadata footer names v2.0.0, linux_arm64 and the extension_version below, read 2026-11-25).",
  "directory": "duckdb-extensions",
  "load_order": [
    "httpfs",
    "avro",
    "iceberg",
    "spatial"
  ],
  "load_order_reason": "iceberg reads manifests through avro and data files through httpfs. With automatic loading off it does not load them itself, so they are loaded first. spatial (geometries, the spheroid distance) stands alone; the parcel nearby Gold reads it (root ADR-0567). H3 is computed in the publisher (h3o): DuckDB's community h3 extension loads only with unsigned extensions allowed.",
